      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T22:19:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, `kFilterNone` does not read the second row. However, some\nInterpolateRow implementations form `src_ptr + src_stride` before the\nzero-fraction early return, including the C and AArch64 NEON versions.\nSince point sampling can now select the final logical row, passing zero\navoids forming an out-of-range pointer, especially with a negative source\nstride.",
      "parentUuid": "505d05cc_561abd8e",
      "revId": "4b3abc0935c28876f6be915cfe2bc3bf5b63774f",
